By providing written notice, theglobe may terminate this Agreement in its sole discretion if one of the following companies (or their subsidiaries) does an "Ownership Change Event": Lycos, Yahoo (including GeoCities, which shall be included even if their proposed merger does not occur), Xoom, Fortune City, Excite, Go Network (including Disney and Infoseek), Snap! (including NBC) and AOL. An "Ownership Change Event" means:
- the acquisition of 50% or more of Boxlot's equity or voting interests;
- a merger or consolidation of Boxlot.

Each party shall maintain insurance, including comprehensive or commercial general liability and products liability insurance (contractual liability included), with respect to its activities under this Agreement in such amounts and with such limits as reasonable and customary in the industry, but with limits not less than the following:

- each occurrence, one million dollars ($1,000,000);
- products/completed operations aggregate, five million dollars ($5,000,000);
- personal and advertising injury, one million dollars ($1,000,000); and
- general aggregate (commercial form only), five million dollars ($5,000,000).
